From: CirrusMusic maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] Debian: adapt Qt 6.10/6.11 APIs to the system Qt 6.8

Applied only to Debian's detached application build worktree. The original
Qt >= 6.10 baseline and the Windows/macOS/Fedora/Arch implementations remain.
Use the existing mkdir(0700) primitive for missing parents, Qt 6.8 row-filter
invalidation, byte/frame conversion and an unbuffered QIODevice PCM pull
adapter. Do not relax existing path/owner/mode/link checks or change decoding.
The build fails with an explicit removal request once Debian meets mainline's
Qt 6.11 APIs, including QAudioSink callbacks. Remove this patch and its build
integration together then.

